  "pages": {
    "index.html": {
      "settings": {
        "main": true,
        "title": "Four Film Composition Styles",
        "meta_descr": "Film composition extends beyond aesthetics—it is a language of emotion and meaning. Through framing, angle, symmetry, and color, filmmakers guide perception, evoke tension, and reveal character. Understanding these visual strategies allows us to see how cinema tells stories not just with words, but with images that speak.\n\n电影构图超越了美学范畴，它是一种情感与意义的语言。导演通过取景、角度、对称与色彩，引导观众的感知，营造张力，并揭示人物特质。理解这些视觉策略，使我们得以体会电影如何以影像而非语言，诉说故事与情感。",
        "header_custom": "",
        "footer_custom": "",
        "html_before": ""
      },
      "components": [
        {
          "alias": false,
          "_styles": {
